hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"68","Muhammad bin Qais narrated: Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, said to me: Go to those people who lead the people in prayer during Ramadan, and command them to perform prostration (sajdah) in Surah Inshiqaq and Surah A'la during the Friday prayer. The son of Abdur Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me a hadith from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he performed prostration in them."
"69","Muhammad bin Muhajir narrated, he heard from Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) that he was telling Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding the prostrations of forgetfulness, that both these prostrations are before the salam. Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) denied this and said, O Ibn Shihab! This information regarding the two prostrations of forgetfulness was narrated to us by Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman."
"70","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, performed prostration in Surah Inshiqaq."
"71","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prostration in Surah Inshiqaq."
